-- X14 (#2185's own defect class, RE-OPENED as fix-round F1, S0) the `display`
-- twin of x12. x12/x13 pin that the auto-print wrap's synthesized reference is
-- not capturable by an interface method named `println`; slice 1 satisfied them
-- by RESPELLING the wrap as `putStrLn (display <e>)` -- which merely MOVED the
-- capture onto `display`, a name users declare constantly for `Pretty`-style
-- interfaces. This row grades the SAME question at the name the respelling
-- introduced, so no future respelling can pay for the pin again.
--
-- MEASURED ON THE SPRINT HEAD a17281e6 (cold-built in this worktree,
-- MEDAKA_STRICT=1): check and build both ACCEPT (exit 0) and the BUILT BINARY
-- prints `HIJACKED` -- the wrap's synthesized `display` silently dispatched
-- through THIS module's `impl Ifc Int`. No diagnostic; a right-looking wrong
-- ANSWER at exit 0 (S0 shape), on a program whose source text never writes
-- `display` at a call site at all.
--
-- FIXED shape: the wrap synthesizes NO name resolved in the user's scope. It
-- calls the PRELUDE's own `println` declaration, re-bound under a name a
-- Medaka identifier can never spell (`autoPrintPinCore`,
-- compiler/driver/main_autoprint.mdk), so the `display` its body reaches is
-- resolved in the PRELUDE's scope -- exactly as a user-written `main =
-- println 7` already was. The built binary must print 7.
--
-- `run` REJECTs BY DESIGN (#1681, mirrors x7/x11/x12/x13): `main` is a non-Unit
-- VALUE and `medaka run` never applies or prints one -- graded BUILD_EXACT for
-- the same reason. Value hand-derived from the literal `main = 7` (the impl's
-- "HIJACKED" must NEVER appear here), not captured.
interface Ifc c where
  display : c -> String

impl Ifc Int where
  display n = "HIJACKED"

main = 7
